<caml:Content xmlns:caml="http://lc.ca.gov/legalservices/schemas/caml.1#"><p>(a)<span class="EnSpace"/>The financial records of a soliciting organization shall be maintained on the basis of generally accepted accounting principles as defined by the American Institute of Certified Public Accountants, the Governmental Accounting Standards Board, or the Financial Accounting Standards Board.</p><p>(b)<span class="EnSpace"/>The disclosure requirement of paragraph (7) of subdivision (a) of Section 17510.3 shall be based on the same accounting principles used to maintain the soliciting organization’s
				  financial records.</p></caml:Content>